module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterE.Section01.ValuesEvenClassical.RankTwoUpper.LinearThreeCover

/-!
# Rank-two classical inputs to E.1.14(1)

The concrete PSL₃ parabolics give a generating family of overgroups of T,
transported through an actual model equivalence. E-generation of its members
has not yet been established. If T interchanges the two parabolics, either
such overgroup is already the whole group and requires a separate argument.

The PSL₃(2^f) and Sp₄(2^f)' upper E-generation calculations remain open;
in particular the binary symplectic case must use the derived subgroup.
This module does not yet assert either upper bound.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
E.1.14(1), printed p.214, citing Aschbacher (1982), Lemma 4.7.
-/
